# CODEOWNERS — JOL Docs (platform documentation hub)
#
# Each line is a file pattern followed by one or more owners; the last match wins.
# NOTE: only teams verified to exist in `journeyoflife-org` are referenced here.
# (The org's teams are: backend, data, devops, frontend, security.)
# Owners are expressed as teams; the accountable human role is named in each
# document's Document-Control block (e.g. "Platform Architect", "Data Protection Officer").

# Default ownership — security governs the documentation hub.
*                                   @journeyoflife-org/security

# Architecture Decision Records — platform architecture + security review.
adr/                                @journeyoflife-org/security @journeyoflife-org/backend

# Architecture diagrams — backend + devops (infrastructure) review.
architecture/                       @journeyoflife-org/backend @journeyoflife-org/devops

# GDPR records of processing and data-flow maps — security (DPO function) review.
gdpr/                               @journeyoflife-org/security

# Compliance crosswalks — security review.
compliance/                         @journeyoflife-org/security

# Security- and governance-sensitive paths.
SECURITY.md                         @journeyoflife-org/security
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                  @journeyoflife-org/security
LICENSE                             @journeyoflife-org/security
.github/CODEOWNERS                  @journeyoflife-org/security
.github/workflows/                  @journeyoflife-org/security

# CI / dependency automation.
.github/dependabot.yml              @journeyoflife-org/security
